{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1538","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Funny Substrings"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarp came up with a new programming language. There are only two types of statements in it: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x := s"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\": assign the variable named "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a string). For example, the statement "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"var := hello"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" assigns the variable named "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"var"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"hello"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the value of a string, not the name of a variable. Between the variable name, the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":":="}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operator and the string contains exactly one space each."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x = a + b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\": assign the variable named "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the concatenation of values of two variables "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, if the program consists of three statements "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a := hello"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b := world"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c = a + b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", then the variable "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" will contain the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"helloworld"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that the program is correct and the variables "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" were previously defined. There is exactly one space between the variable names and the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"="}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operators. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All variable names and strings only consist of lowercase letters of the English alphabet and do not exceed $$$5$$$ characters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The result of the program is the number of occurrences of string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"haha"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the string that was written to the variable in the last statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Polycarp was very tired while inventing that language. He asks you to implement it. Your task is — for given program statements calculate the number of occurrences of string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"haha"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the last assigned variable."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^3$$$). Then $$$t$$$ test cases follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 50$$$) — the number of statements in the program. All variable names and strings are guaranteed to consist only of lowercase letters of the English alphabet and do not exceed $$$5$$$ characters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is followed by $$$n$$$ lines describing the statements in the format described above. It is guaranteed that the program is correct."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each set of input data, output the number of occurrences of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"haha"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" substring in the string that was written to the variable in the last statement."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n6\na := h\nb := aha\nc = a + b\nc = c + c\ne = c + c\nd = a + c\n15\nx := haha\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\nx = x + x\n1\nhaha := hah\n5\nhaahh := aaaha\nahhhh = haahh + haahh\nhaahh = haahh + haahh\nahhhh = ahhhh + haahh\nahhaa = haahh + ahhhh\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n32767\n0\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case the resulting value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"hhahahaha"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"1538E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1538/problem/E"}